🚀 Week 3 – Day 5 Constructors & Inheritance in Java ☕

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧠 Introduction

In Java:

✔ Constructors initialize objects
✔ Inheritance allows one class to reuse another class’s properties and methods

👉 These are core OOP concepts and are frequently asked in interviews.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🏗️ 1. Constructors

A constructor is a special method that is automatically called when an object is created.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📌 Characteristics

✔ Constructor name must be the same as class name
✔ No return type (not even `void`)
✔ Executes automatically when using `new`

---

📌 Default Constructor

```java id="c1"
class Student {
    Student() {
        System.out.println("Constructor called");
    }
}
```

---

📌 Parameterized Constructor

```java id="c2"
class Student {
    String name;

    Student(String n) {
        name = n;
    }
}
```

---

💻 Complete Example

```java id="c3"
class Student {
    String name;
    int age;

    Student(String name, int age) {
        this.name = name;
        this.age = age;
    }

    void display() {
        System.out.println(name + " " + age);
    }
}
```

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧬 2. Inheritance

Inheritance allows one class to acquire fields and methods of another class.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📌 Syntax

```java id="i1"
class Child extends Parent {
}
```

---

📌 Example

```java id="i2"
class Animal {
    void sound() {
        System.out.println("Animal makes a sound");
    }
}

class Dog extends Animal {
    void bark() {
        System.out.println("Dog barks");
    }
}
```

---

▶️ Using Inherited Methods

```java id="i3"
Dog d = new Dog();
d.sound();
d.bark();
```

---

📊 Types of Inheritance in Java

* Single Inheritance ✔
* Multilevel Inheritance ✔
* Hierarchical Inheritance ✔
* Multiple Inheritance ❌ (not with classes)

---

🔹 super Keyword

Used to refer to parent class members.

```java id="i4"
super();
super.variable;
super.method();
```

---

🎯 Advantages of Inheritance

✔ Code reuse
✔ Reduced duplication
✔ Easier maintenance

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Constructor name different from class name
❌ Using constructor like a normal method
❌ Forgetting `extends` keyword

---

🧠 Real-World Example

* `Vehicle` → Parent class
* `Car` → Child class
* `Bike` → Child class

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📚 Key Takeaways

✔ Constructors initialize objects
✔ Constructors can be default or parameterized
✔ Inheritance enables code reuse
✔ Child classes inherit parent methods and fields
✔ `super` accesses parent class members

